                  "purpose":  "Documented expected-truth table for the cache-honesty mock fixtures (WI-0). States which ASSIGNED reviewer SHOULD show complete/incomplete per campaign per cert. Downstream WI-1 (red repro) and WI-11 (end-to-end proof) assert the rendered who-completed/who-did-not against this file.",
                  "planItem":  "WI-0",
                  "planIdMapping":  {
                                        "camp-active-001":  "camp-ch-active-001",
                                        "camp-completed-001":  "camp-ch-completed-001",
                                        "camp-transition-001":  "camp-ch-transition-001",
                                        "reassignment-fixture":  "camp-ch-reassign-001"
                                    },
                  "planIdMappingRationale":  "The plan literal IDs camp-active-001 / camp-completed-001 ALREADY EXIST in the live mock seed-data.json with conflicting data and are load-bearing for existing mock tests (Tests/Integration/Test-SailPointWorkflow.ps1, Tests/Smoke/Invoke-SmokeTest.ps1). Per the additive prime directive they are NOT mutated; a new collision-free camp-ch-* namespace (ch = cache-honesty) is introduced instead. Downstream WI-1/WI-11 consume this truth file, so the IDs are decoupled from the plan literals.",
                  "classifierRules":  "Mirrors Group-SPAuditDecisions (Modules/SP.Audit/SP.AuditReportCore.psm1 switch at ~line 404): decision in {APPROVE,APPROVED,CERTIFY} AND justification/comment does NOT contain idNowAutoApproved =\u003e APPROVED (decided). decision in {APPROVE,...} WITH comment containing idNowAutoApproved =\u003e PENDING (auto-approved; counts as NOT complete). decision in {REVOKE,REVOKED,DENY,REJECT,EXCEPTION} =\u003e REVOKED (decided). null/empty/missing/UNDECIDED decision =\u003e PENDING (genuinely undecided). reviewerName is read from reviewedBy.name (OBJECT form), which is null for pending items.",
                  "reviewerCompleteRule":  "A cert\u0027s ASSIGNED reviewer SHOULD show COMPLETE iff that cert has zero undecided items (no null-decision AND no idNowAutoApproved), else INCOMPLETE. Attribution is by item.CertificationId -\u003e cert.reviewer (the sealed assigned reviewer), NEVER item.reviewedBy (null for pending items, which today collapses every undecided item into a single (Unassigned) row).",
                  "completeFormula":  "shouldShowComplete == (undecidedCount == 0 AND autoApprovedCount == 0); shouldAppearInIncompleteList == (NOT shouldShowComplete AND NOT reassignedAway)."
              },
